  triage:title "The sprint owns paths in crates/sc-ai/**, crates/sc-jev-py/**, docs/sc-ai/** and" ;
  triage:description "The sprint owns paths in crates/sc-ai/**, crates/sc-jev-py/**, docs/sc-ai/** and docs/sc-jev-py/**, but its `requirements` list omits two crate-level ids. REQ-SAG-0703 (sc-ai install documentation; r-3b edits the sc-ai docs and the sc-publish.md crate-order lines) and REQ-SAG-0803 (sc-jev-py first release on all five channels; r-3b edits the rendered release inputs and release/**) are not named. Every other row in both crate requirements files is listed. REQ-SAG-0134 (cargo-tree-gates.sh mimalloc rows, which this sprint extends) and REQ-SAG-0620 (one RunResponse serialization printed by every consumer, per D3.2) are also in the sprint's subject area and unlisted. Recommendation: Add REQ-SAG-0703 and REQ-SAG-0803 to the sprint front-matter `requirements` list. Add REQ-SAG-0134 and REQ-SAG-0620 as well, or record in the sprint doc why they are not constraints. Then record a requirement_check for each." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-a-refine" ;
